    "body": "Status update (@farre and I are working on this to align with Gecko or Chromium or both):\r\n\r\n- 958e7eb: a blocked `fetch()` response gets a null body. Allowed ones keep theirs, so a service worker can pass them on.\r\n- aba078b: sniffed audio, video, and images are allowed regardless of the media request state.\r\n- 578e394: FedCM is exempt for now (see my previous comment).\r\n- 173b75d: restores #1442's nosniff + blocklisted check.\r\n- Tests: web-platform-tests/wpt#64714.\r\n\r\nTo do:\r\n\r\n- @annevk, thanks for the AI review. 173b75d covers the nosniff blocker and [wpt#64714](https://github.com/web-platform-tests/wpt/pull/64714) updates `expected_block`. Still need to go through the rest.\r\n- Remaining differences with Gecko/Chromium: the DASH/HLS/VTT and `audio/mpeg`-style allowances, the JSON check on decoded text, the fallback encoding, and tying \"subsequent\" to a URL that sniffed as media.\r\n- Gecko still blocks beacon responses instead of filtering them, so that needs a bug.",
