    "updated_at": "2026-11-05T10:32:06Z",
    "body": "Media findings:\r\n\r\nUnlabeled responses to media requests are blocked unless they sniff as audio or video (step 8). Gecko does this; Chromium allows them. Unlabeled responses to non-media requests are allowed in the spec, Gecko, and Chromium, so the bigger gap is annevk/orb#28. Step 8 doesn't cost compat for media, though, so it fits ORB's objective.\r\n\r\nOur proposal is to keep step 8 and align with Gecko otherwise:\r\n\r\n- Allow `application/vnd.apple.mpegurl`, `audio/mpegurl`, `application/dash+xml`, and `text/vtt` without sniffing, and remove them from the never-sniffed list. Gecko does this ([bug 1698040](https://bugzilla.mozilla.org/show_bug.cgi?id=1698040)) and Chromium safelists them.\r\n- Allow `audio/mpeg`, `audio/aac`, `audio/aacp`, and `multipart/x-mixed-replace` without sniffing, instead of never-sniffing them as the PR does now. Some MP3 servers aren't sniffable mid-stream. That's what Gecko does; Chromium safelists all `audio/*` and `video/*`.\r\n- Add Gecko's media signatures to mimesniff's audio or video pattern matching: MPEG-TS, ADTS (whatwg/mimesniff#114), more MP4 brands (whatwg/mimesniff#149), FLAC, Matroska, and `#EXTM3U`.\r\n- Sniff more than 1024 bytes: 1445 as mimesniff does, so 320 kbps MP3 frames fit, and up to 8096 for ADTS as Gecko does (https://github.com/whatwg/mimesniff/issues/218).\r\n- Sniff playlists at each step, since entries can point to arbitrary cross-origin URLs, including nested playlists.\r\n- Block `text/plain` with nosniff, as Chromium does and the spec does since 173b75d. Gecko will drop its exception ([bug 2089487](https://bugzilla.mozilla.org/show_bug.cgi?id=2089487)). Tested in web-platform-tests/wpt#64714.\r\n- Chromium would need to add step 8, after the new mimesniff signatures land so unlabeled HLS segments and MP3 streams don't break.\r\n\r\nDoes this work for Chromium and WebKit?",
    "author_association": "MEMBER",
